    "cover_text": "Inside the newly furnished hall stood shelves lined with rusted iron carts and wooden carriages that had served the town's daily life for nearly a century. As the first light from the lamps shifted across the floor tiles from amber to a deeper orange hour-by-hour throughout the long winter nights of the season between late January and the first frost of April above the Great Lakes (or wherever winter had settled in this frozen valley), visitors traced the layout of the old street map with their fingertips. An elderly keeper of the museum's history pointed to a single sign made of local stone that listed the names of every ferry service and carriage owner who had once stood there. \"Look,\" she said gently as she showed them to a window displaying the silhouette of the current ferryboat against the icy black water. \"Though everything has changed since 1850 for the sake of speed and safety...\" The museum opened a new room about the history of local transportation. It felt as though",
